index 0000000..c1c9bc9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/sinj.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Symbolic residual injection
+
+Symbolic injection adds a runtime vector to selected Qwen2 residual streams.
+The public API is `llama_set_adapter_sinj()`. Each entry selects a layer,
+`attn`, `mlp`, or `block` point, a gain, optional RMS scaling, and a position
+range. Passing no entries clears all injections.
+
+Sidecars use format `symbolic-vector-sidecar-v1`. Each vector is a finite,
+unit-RMS list with exactly `dim` values; `dim` must match the model embedding
+size. `at` may be `"all"` or `"current"` for every position, or `"here"` with
+a `positions` list. Position lists are merged into contiguous ranges. The
+example is schematic; replace the vector placeholder with exactly `dim`
+floats.
+
+```json
+{
+  "format": "symbolic-vector-sidecar-v1",
+  "model": "model.gguf",
+  "vectors": [{
+    "sid": 1,
+    "headwords": "love joy happy",
+    "contrast": "hate anger sad",
+    "layer": 12,
+    "point": "block",
+    "gain": 4,
+    "at": "all",
+    "dim": 1536,
+    "vector": ["1536 unit-RMS float values"],
+    "rms_scale": true
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+Load one at startup with `--sinj sidecar.json` or
+`--symbolic-file symbolic.txt`. Both options can be used together. JSON
+`at: "current"` remains unbounded, like the torch sidecar semantics. In the
+text format, `current` means decode-only: injections are disabled for batches
+with more than one token and enabled for single-token decode batches.
+
+The server exposes `GET /sinj` and `POST /sinj`; POST accepts the JSON sidecar
+format, and an empty `vectors` array clears the entries.
+
+The extractor can create a sidecar:
+
+```text
+llama-sinj-extract -m model.gguf --text "love joy happy" \
+  --contrast "hate anger sad" --layer 12 --point block --gain 4 \
+  -o sidecar.json
+```
+
+KV cache entries computed before a change keep the old injection. Clear or
+recompute the prompt after changing entries.
